    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0847" n="751" xml:id="pg751"/>

                <head>No. 483.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 27,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 109.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A copy of your dispatch, relative to the
                    condemnation of the assassins of Rev. John L. Stephens, having been communicated
                    to the American Board of Commissioners for Foreign Missions, Boston, I transmit
                    for your information a copy of a letter, dated the 19th instant, addressed to
                    this Department by Mr. Clark, the secretary, expressing, on behalf of the board,
                    much satisfaction because of the prompt attention given by you to this case, and
                    of the efficient measures adopted by the Mexican authorities.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d485-a1.xml" xpointer="d485-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
